{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1467313-finding-lost-kinfolk","id":1467313,"title":"Finding lost kinfolk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-09T18:29:57-08:00","id":1467313,"title":"Finding lost kinfolk","content":"How would Garou go about searching a city for suspected lost kinfolk, if they have no leads or ID? Something akin to a reverse kinfetch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T23:22:00-08:00","id":1467327,"title":"","content":"Do they have something owned/worn by the kinfolk that provides scent? If so, they can begin tracking. Now the urban environment presents challenges to scent tracking alone, but it would be a start available to any Garou.<br /> <br /> The Rite of the Questing Stone (level one mystic) is probably the most obvious response. As long as you know the name, you can get the direction of where that person is. You won't know it exactly, but once you get to an area, it'll become much easier to narrow it down.<br /> <br /> The level two Ragabash Gift Pulse of the Prey provides an unerring sense of direction to track any prey as fast it can travel as long as the Garou knows <i>anything</i> about the prey.<br /> <br /> Not knowing more specifics about the scenario, this is what immediately comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T07:28:44-08:00","id":1467354,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> is correct, however, I understood the scenario quite differently.<br /> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26645_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26645\" data-vbnamecard=\"26645\">pwtucker</a> you should clarify, if the garou are looking for a specific kin-person whose whereabouts aren't known, or if they are trying to find any person who is kinfolk, but has no clue about garou society and lives apart from it for, like the 2nd generation or something....<br /> <br /> For the later scenario, there isn't much to go on. &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; is a separate roll for each subject, and therefore false positive and false negative are a likely outcome, especially for the botches that statistically are bound to happen.<br /> The Bone Gnawer Gift &quot;On Patrol&quot; might, as I read it, provide a means of using &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; more easily in an urban setting, but it might only detect beings with wyrm taint, and then allow to use other Gifts like &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; over greater distances and such. So, to find kinfolk per s\u00e9 it might not be the optimal thing to do....<br /> <br /> <br /> If one Glaswalker had the DNA sequence of some garou and kinfolk in a database and access to a variety of DNA samples, he could find family relationships and therefore narrow down to whom he would have to send a Philodox to sniff around, literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T08:11:32-08:00","id":1467358,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick feedback. Should have been more specific up front.<br /> <br /> Here's the situation: the PC's have moved to a city whose old caern was destroyed and lost five years ago. A new one has been opened, but most of the old local kinfolk connections have been lost. The PC's would like to try and locate those lost kinfolk, but with the original Garou dead, they (and I) aren't sure how they'd go about locating the kin. <br /> <br /> Sounds like their best bet might be to dig up extended family outside the city or find one or two Garou who fled the original caern. I just wanted to check if there was any kind of ritual, spirit, or otherwise mystical way of going about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T13:20:19-08:00","id":1467376,"title":"","content":"There is a level three mystic Rite in the second edition Players Guide called the Rite of Blood Kin. It allows the ritemaster to identify unknown kinfolk close to him. Each success rolled gives the ritemaster the identity of one previously unknown Kinfolk within 100 miles of the Garou. I don't think that rite has been included anywhere else, but you can probably find it online somewhere if you don't have access to that book.<br /> <br /> Other possibilities in that scenario might be to summon Ancestor Spirits of dead Garou the previous caern who <i>might</i> be able to provide names of blood relatives. Similarly, there may still be spirits previously affiliated with the caern that are still around who can also provide information.<br /> <br /> There could also be old fashioned detective work using whatever was known about the previous sept, and identify potential kinfolk of the dead Garou that way. Know any of the human names of the old Garou? Search through birth registers, land ownership, and such should be able to identify family members, and once you have some names you can start getting more names. Look for other things in common like business partnerships, places of employment, volunteer organizations, and other groups that might be a result of kinfolk covering needed tasks for the sept. Get use of a PC's Investigation skill.<br /> <br /> A combination of the above to collect information followed by use of the Pulse of the Prey or Rite of the Questing Stone to locate them, and Scent of True Form to confirm kinfolk status should allow the PCs to discover enough existing kinfolk to accomplish whatever they wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T18:18:05-08:00","id":1467398,"title":"","content":"If the PCs can access any sample DNA from the Garou in the lost sept and have enough Resources to pull it, they can also do things like offer on their own those Ancestry DNA tests to townsfolk.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of money if they try everyone, but coupled with other methods can help a lot in finding lost relatives, with the added benefit of every test improving the effectiveness of the entire database.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T14:24:50-08:00","id":1467725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1467313-finding-lost-kinfolk?p=1467376#post1467376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other possibilities in that scenario might be to summon Ancestor Spirits of dead Garou the previous caern ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that even possible?<br /> Ancestor Spirits are of Breed, Tribe or Auspice and embody aspects of these concepts and while they often do have the appearance and possibly memories of specific dead ancestors, like the King of House Winter Snow, whom Albrecht met, it is not like any dead garou becomes an ancestor spirit. Or is it?<br /> I know that Garou who disconnect from the material due to staying to long in the Umbra are rules-wise considered to be akin to Ancestor spirits, even if they aren't really.<br /> Also, Wewaupet might be considered an Ancestor Spirit, but his soul is tied to the world by the first version of the Spell of Life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T23:34:29-08:00","id":1467767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1467313-finding-lost-kinfolk?p=1467725#post1467725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that even possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think it would be up to the ST to decide whether the Ancestor spirits of the dead Garou could identify any extant relatives of their lineage. If the previous Garou of the sept had any Ancestors background, then those Ancestor spirits might know of any relatives those Garou had.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the nature of Ancestor spirits, they certainly have a link to living Garou. Whether that provides any useful knowledge depends on the ST.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T04:24:29-08:00","id":1467864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1467313-finding-lost-kinfolk?p=1467767#post1467767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of the nature of Ancestor spirits, they certainly have a link to living Garou. Whether that provides any useful knowledge depends on the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd limit that to Homid/Lupus Ancestor spirits, and tribe ancestor spirits, but true, they would be able to provide information.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}